{
 "_summary": [
  "A/B test of a second bounded retry ('reorder') added to the step that turns the planner's high-level plans into legal robot moves (the realizer in eval/realize.py, strict_moves).",
  "The retry targets ordering failures where a robot stands on another move's destination cell and the plan itself moves it later -- including the pure swap: a stopper must be placed on the very cell its future bouncer still occupies, so the bouncer's approach leg is executed first (analysis had estimated 4 such swaps, idx 0/1/62/105).",
  "The retry is deterministic and bounded (at most one reorder per blocked move, no search) and only ever runs AFTER the default schedule has already failed; it reorders the plan's own declared moves and never invents new ones.",
  "All 112 plans of the matched 150 that the stored benchmark (comparison_backward_postfix2.json) already realized return exactly the same move count as before: 0 regressions, 112/112 identical counts.",
  "Of the 38 stored failures, 7 now execute fully into legal move sequences (idx [0, 1, 30, 92, 105, 108, 121]); every one was replayed move-by-move under the game physics (simulate.slide) with the full joint state: 7/7 legal, target reached.",
  "The newly fixed plans average 11.86 moves at mean regret 3.43 extra moves over the shortest possible solution (d*); per-instance costs are in per_instance.",
  "3 of the 4 predicted swaps (idx 0, 1, 105) are among the fixes; idx 62 is not: its plan also parks two different robots permanently-in-sequence on one cell ((0,12) is both Blue's stopper post and Green's landing cell), and untangling that needs a robot to arrive, be consumed, and depart between another segment's two legs -- beyond the sanctioned single-reorder vocabulary, so it fails cleanly as before.",
  "4 additional ordering failures (idx 30, 92, 108, 121, all from the same 16-instance 'blocked by a plan robot moving later' class) fall to the same retry.",
  "All 150 plans regenerate bit-identically to the stored run (150/150 abstract costs match); the 38 failing plans were additionally cross-checked against the pickled plans of the diagnosis run (38/38 agree on the new outcome and count).",
  "With the retry on by default the benchmark solve count rises from 112 to 119 of 150 (74% -> 79%); it is enabled inside the default two_phase=True realizer since there are no regressions."
 ],
